{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cg6UBLdEsZDdqpXQxbkG2", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "```\nTable 3 reports the estimates, and they point to a clear role for reviewer identity. In column 2, the coefficient on the identity-disclosed indicator is 0.18 (SE = 0.04). It remains substantial after we add product fixed effects in column 3, where it is 0.15 (SE = 0.05). Identity also conditions the effect of a review: the interaction with reviewer tenure is 0.09 (SE = 0.03) in column 4. Star rating matters throughout, with a coefficient of 0.42 (SE = 0.02) across all specifications, yet identity adds to it rather than being absorbed by it. Model fit improves accordingly, as R-squared rises from 0.31 to 0.47 across the columns. All coefficients are significant at the 1% level except the interaction, which is significant at the 5% level.\n```\n\nI kept every number and its order unchanged, and there are no citations in the paragraph. Two edits go slightly beyond sentence-level polish, so check them against your intent. \"Identity adds to it rather than being absorbed by it\" is an interpretive claim, which the stability of the 0.18 and 0.15 estimates supports but your original did not state. \"Model fit improves accordingly\" implies the R-squared gain comes from the identity terms. If the gain also reflects the fixed effects, soften or cut that phrase."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1881, "cache_read_input_tokens": 1496, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1881}, "output_tokens": 2, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "19b6103d-cbfc-505f-8dc1-c40cc8379cf6", "uuid": "